// Second round the owner approved on 14 Oct 2026 ("yes add them and fix the
// false alarm"). Four scam types the engine scored NOT A SCAM, the warning
// trick, and one false alarm:
//
//  A. Widow / romance inheritance: a stranger ("a lonely widow", "my late
//     husband left me gold") asks you to help invest, manage or receive it.
//  B. Gold-mine partner: a stranger who owns a gold mine wants a partner,
//     investor or buyer for a share of the profit.
//  C. Cheap gold bars: kilos of gold bars, dust or nuggets below the market
//     price, an "urgent sale", "documents ready".
//  D. The 419 business proposal: "worth $10.4M, 100% risk free, confidential,
//     reply for details", even before any ask.
//  E. A scam that opens with "beware of scammers" and then makes its own
//     pitch. Real warnings that only describe or quote a scam stay quiet.
//
// False alarm: "صندوق الاستثمار حقق عائد 8% هذا العام حسب التقرير السنوي" (a
// fund's annual report) scored SCAM 55 as an investment pitch. A report, news
// item, question or plain statement about returns, with no invitation,
// guarantee, contact ask or pressure aimed at the reader, is not a pitch.
//
// The "r3-" cases at the end come from the hardening round the same day: the
// scams two independent hunters wrote that the first version still missed
// (typos, Arabic dialect, "my uncle owns a mine", "LBMA minus 12%", "an
// investor with $50 million needs a local partner", warnings with no
// punctuation), and the real messages it wrongly called scams (central-bank
// gold news, a jeweller's volume discount, a quote at spot plus a premium,
// named business contacts, dirham property deals, a licensed mining company's
// MoU, fund statements, market roundups, victims' stories).
